# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# setup: iderunboards
# board: discover
# Two boards on one desk, and choosing between them.
#
# Both are the same make and both call themselves tiku, so the shell
# names the second one apart; that pair of names is what the editor
# offers.  A program lights the lamp of whatever board runs it, so each
# board's own /dev/led0 afterwards says whether it was the one -- which
# is the whole question two boards raise.  The dark state both start
# from is MADE here, by running the program that puts the lamp out on
# each board in turn: the same program, sent to two places.
wait 200
note connect devices through TikuDesktop before opening TikuBasic
click 264 8
wait 10
menu-pick Connect to nRF54L15
wait 300
click 264 8
wait 10
menu-pick Connect to nRF54LM20B
wait 300
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Development
wait 4
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 150
expect-title Project
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
expect-title Open
click 400 220
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
expect-no-title Open
click-window Project
wait 8
note quiet.bas puts the lamp out; chosen before the menu opens, so the
note offers and the choosing are one visit
key Down
wait 6
key Down
wait 8
note a legacy project board entry cannot override the desktop default
click 264 8
wait 8
menu-pick Default device:
wait 8
expect-menu nrf54l15
expect-menu nrf54lm20b
menu-pick nrf54lm20b
wait 10
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Run quiet.bas on nrf54lm20b
wait 250
note and now the same program to the OTHER board
click-window Project
wait 8
click 264 8
wait 8
menu-pick Default device:
wait 8
menu-pick nrf54l15
wait 10
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Run quiet.bas on nrf54l15
wait 250
note both lamps are out, and each was put out by a run sent to it
expect-read /devices/nrf54lm20b/dev/led0 0
expect-read /devices/nrf54l15/dev/led0 0
note now blink.bas, the one that lights a lamp, to one board only
click-window Project
wait 8
key Up
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Run blink.bas on nrf54l15
wait 250
note lit on the board that was chosen
expect-read /devices/nrf54l15/dev/led0 1
note and dark on the one that was not: a program went to ONE board
expect-read /devices/nrf54lm20b/dev/led0 0
note Run and Save both follow the desktop default
click-window Project
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Run blink.bas on nrf54l15|Save on nrf54l15|
click-window Project
wait 10
click 264 8
wait 8
menu-pick Default device:
wait 8
expect-menu nrf54l15
expect-menu nrf54lm20b
quit
